What the Design Shows
The design, which is a polished social media carousel, indicates that it is meant to promote engagement. This is because it has a consistent brand color scheme, two fonts (one for headers, another for regular text), and aligns elements to create a visual hierarchy. The design utilizes Canva’s frames to maintain uniformity in images. There is negative space to allow for maximum readability. The design transforms an ordinary idea into an outstanding visual. 
One Thing Found Interesting/Difficult:

    Interesting Feature: Learning how to utilize the "Magic Switch" to resize the project instantly, according to the specific social media site (Instagram Story, LinkedIn Post, etc.), without having to manually arrange the elements, is an interesting feature, especially considering how efficient it is. 
    Difficult Aspect: The most difficult part is creating the perfect balance. Manually aligning the elements to ensure they are not too close to the edge of the page, while at the same time ensuring they are "spaced" from each other, requires constant switching between "Position" and "Tidy Up."
